 \subsection{Computational structure and intended use}
 \label{sec:cost}
 
-\Full{} stores all local and cross-community channels, and its work per event grows with node degree \citep{kuryliak2025simulating}. \TS{} stores the local graphs and an $M\times M$ matrix of aggregate weights. The workshop paper discusses this reduction in the information stored for cross-community contacts \citep{kuryliak2025towards}. Its importance depends on the problem. Replacing many individual cross-community edges by one weight can reduce storage. If only a few such edges exist, this saving may be small, and the local graphs still have to be stored.
